DTP (Dynamic Trunking Protocol): allow cisco switches to dynamically switch their interfaces status (access/trunk) (for trunk it needs to be 2 cisco switches, otherwise
it will be automatically access port). It's enable by default, so technically we dont need to do switchport mode access or switchport mode trunk, but we should
disable it for security purposes. DTP can be put in desirable mode (will actively form a trunk if another switchport is connected in trunk mode, dynamic desirable 
mode or dynamic auto mode)or auto mode (will not actively try to form a trunk, but will do if it's connected if another switchport is connected in trunk mode or 
dynamic desirable mode.

VTP (VLAN Trunking Protocol): allows you to configure vlans on a central vtp server.
